# Build results. The directory also holds the settings and the log of a build
# started from here, which the program keeps next to its executable.
/dist/

# A program built at the top of the tree rather than into dist/: the test task
# compiles one there to run the command line against, and a copy left behind by
# hand has no business in a commit either. The build itself writes to dist/.
/SDAutoLogin
/SDAutoLogin.exe

# CMake build tree
/build/
/build-*/

# Runtime data, when the program is started from the repository root: with no
# executable of its own to sit next to, it falls back to the working directory.
/config.json
/logs/

# A signing key left at the top of the tree. keygen no longer writes here — the
# private half goes to the per-user configuration directory, and the release
# build is given its text in the environment — but a key that was made by an
# earlier version, or put here by hand, must never be committed. A key in the
# repository signs whatever anyone asks it to.
/signing.key

# Key material anywhere else in the tree, whatever it is named. A key written
# by hand, or one named by SDAUTOLOGIN_SIGNING_KEY_FILE, is not at the top of
# the tree and would otherwise be added by "git add -A" without a word. Once a
# key is in a commit it is in the history for good, so the pattern goes by
# extension: nothing this repository holds ends in one of these.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
